A("**Method.** A script (`extract_index.py`, kept beside this index) parsed every report file header-by-header: finding IDs and exact titles from the `##`/`###`/`####` headers (both the `ID / Title / Category N` and the `ID — Title` families, plus Launchstation Round 3’s detail headers), and Category/Effort/Risk/Confidence from each finding’s own field lines (bold and unbolded variants, fields carried on the Benefit line, and Launchstation Round 3’s at-a-glance table cross-check). "
  "The running extraction table is preserved as `index-scratch.tsv`. Every ID was extracted exactly once (zero duplicate headers across files), and every allocated block came out complete (001–max contiguous for Launchstation, POPSLoader, SMS, PS2-Servers and Cross; RiptOPL complete within its allocated blocks 001…367 / 400…530 / 600…605) — the counts in §1.3 are the extraction’s, and they match the expected figures exactly. "
  "Statuses were not parsed mechanically: each REVISED/WITHDRAWN assignment was transcribed by hand from the SUMMARY addenda and the round files’ revision/revalidation/settlement sections listed in §4. Cross-checks performed: RiptOPL-066’s and SMS-057/SMS-060’s mechanisms, LAUNCHSTATION-119’s macro and LAUNCHSTATION-136’s memset line, and PS2SERVERS-069’s helper were already parent-verified in the rounds; this index re-verified no code — it is an index of the reports, not a re-audit.")
