  "(2) `Sable-POPSLoader-ROUND7.md` tarball section (historical): as originally delivered, only T01…T06 had been renumbered into the text (as POPSLOADER-071…076 headings, -076 truncated) and T07…T26 existed nowhere — the extractor’s R7-T mapping handler (strict benefit order, Tnn → POPSLOADER-(070+nn)) extracted nothing further and POPSLOADER-077…096 were absent from the previous index. **Closed by the completion pass:** the delivered file now carries POPSLOADER-071…107 as ordinary `##` headings, extracted by the normal heading parser; the R7-T handler is retained in the extractor but matches nothing in the current file, and -076’s fields (unparseable before, because its body was truncated in the source) now extract in full. "
  "(3) `Sable-RiptOPL-ROUND9-THIRDPARTY-B.md` (2 rows, RIPTOPL-600…601): the same index-table + `### Title: …` block shape as (1); the extractor pairs blocks to table rows in file order — exact-title pairing is impossible because the table’s short title for -601 drops the word “PSUManager” that its block title carries, while -600’s two titles are identical. Titles/Categories are the table’s; Effort/Risk/Confidence come from the bodies (both findings complete). "
  "(4) `Sable-VERIFICATION-NEW-FINDINGS.md` (6 rows: RIPTOPL-602; SMS-183, SMS-184; POPSLOADER-108; PS2SERVERS-114, PS2SERVERS-115): the verification phase’s own findings file mixes four repos in one file under standard headings; the extractor derives each row’s repo from the ID prefix. SMS-183/SMS-184 are renumbered from the SMS verification pass’s candidate labels SMS-230/SMS-231 (mapping recorded in the file’s header and in §4). "
